# Demo fixture for Project 2 Phase 4. Copy it into a scratch directory to
# watch the confusion defence work.
#
# It is the same pin as the repository's own .npmrc, applied to a scope whose
# package -- @babel/core -- really does exist on the public registry. That is
# the point: the install below fails even though the package is sitting right
# there on npmjs.org. If npm fell back to the public registry, it would
# succeed.
@babel:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com/
